text Fuko isn't taking it easy even during the short period before the festival.
text Even so, more and more people are ignoring her every day.
text And every time, she stands helplessly embracing her starfish...
setvar strS[1001] = "CGFU40"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 30
setimg CGFU40.png
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text ...looking at the back of the unresponsive student getting further and further away.
sound 4ER.aac
text @[{$lnmA}]
text Fu-chan, I'm sure it will go well next time.
text If it wasn't for {$lnmA}, I don't know if I would have the will to keep staying.
text I can't thank her enough for being here and continuing to encourage Fuko.
text ......
text If Fuko can meet Kouko-san and say "Congratulations" to her...
text We may not have to keep on enduring this.
text Fuko's having to try so hard only because she thinks her voice wouldn't reach her sister.
text So if we can lift that weight off her shoulders, maybe she'll open up to other things, and us as well.
text Then maybe even she can have a happy school life.
text @[Tomoya]
text (That has to happen.)
text @[Tomoya]
text (The days of you working through physical and emotional suffering will have to come to an end on the day of the festival.)
text @[Tomoya]
text (Let's make it that way, Fuko.)
text I whisper as my eyes follow Fuko's back as she runs toward another student.
